minkowski-signs-d11fa6d6.interpretation:
The equation $T^{\mu
u} = g^{\mu\alpha} g^{
u eta} T_{\alpha eta}$ expresses the standard tensor calculus operation of raising indices. The tensor $T_{\alpha eta}$ represents a rank-2 covariant tensor (frequently the stress-energy-momentum tensor), while $g^{\mu\alpha}$ and $g^{
u eta}$ are components of the contravariant (inverse) metric tensor satisfying $g^{\mu\alpha} g_{\alpha\lambda} = \delta^\mu_\lambda$. The dummy indices $\alpha$ and $ eta$ are summed from $0$ to $3$ in four-dimensional spacetime, yielding the fully contravariant tensor $T^{\mu
u}$.

minkowski-signs-d11fa6d6.conceptual_definition:
The contravariant components of a second-rank tensor $T^{\mu
u}$ are obtained by contracting the covariant tensor components $T_{\alpha eta}$ with two inverse metric tensors $g^{\mu\alpha}$ and $g^{
u eta}$ via the Einstein summation convention. This operation represents the musical isomorphism applied twice to map dual tangent space vectors (1-forms) to tangent space vectors.
